#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:1
msgid "Compile-Only Tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:3
msgid ""
"`python -m tilelang.tools.compile_only` lowers a TileLang program to "
"inspectable kernel source without running it. No GPU, CUDA driver, or device "
"compilation is required: the tool stops after `tilelang.lower(..., "
"enable_device_compile=False)` and writes the generated kernel source to a "
"file. It backs the TileLang integration in [Compiler Explorer](https://"
"godbolt.org) and is equally useful for inspecting locally what `lower()` "
"produces for a kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:11
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:13
msgid ""
"The tool ships with the standard TileLang installation and has no optional "
"dependencies. The default `c` target works on any machine, including CPU-"
"only hosts. `--target cuda` requires a wheel whose CUDA codegen FFI is "
"compiled in: Linux wheels include it and can emit CUDA source without a GPU "
"present, while macOS Metal wheels do not and fail with a clear `CUDA codegen "
"FFI missing` message instead of an `AttributeError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:20
msgid "Quick Start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:22
msgid ""
"Write a self-contained example that defines a kernel but never launches it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:24
msgid ""
"# example.py\n"
"import tilelang\n"
"import tilelang.language as T\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@tilelang.jit\n"
"def add(A, B):\n"
"    N = 64\n"
"    A: T.Tensor((N,), T.float16)\n"
"    B: T.Tensor((N,), T.float16)\n"
"    C = T.empty((N,), T.float16)\n"
"    with T.Kernel(1, threads=64):\n"
"        for i in T.Parallel(N):\n"
"            C[i] = A[i] + B[i]\n"
"    return C\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:42
msgid "Compile it to CPU C source:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:44
msgid ""
"python -I -m tilelang.tools.compile_only --output_file out.c example.py\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:48
msgid "`out.c` then contains the generated kernel source:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:50
msgid ""
"// tilelang target: {\"kind\":\"c\",\"tag\":\"\",\"keys\":[\"cpu\"],\"host\":"
"{\"kind\":\"c\",\"tag\":\"\",\"keys\":[\"cpu\"]}}\n"
"#include <tl_templates/cpp/common.h>\n"
"\n"
"#ifdef __cplusplus\n"
"extern \"C\"\n"
"#endif\n"
"int32_t add_kernel(half* A, half* B, half* C);\n"
"#ifdef __cplusplus\n"
"extern \"C\"\n"
"#endif\n"
"int32_t add_kernel(half* A, half* B, half* C) {\n"
"  for (int32_t i = 0; i < 8; ++i) {\n"
"    *(half8*)(C + (i * 8)) = (*(half8*)(A + (i * 8)) + *(half8*)(B + (i * "
"8)));\n"
"  }\n"
"  return 0;\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:69
msgid ""
"CUDA source generation works the same way and still needs no GPU; the "
"architecture is pinned instead of detected:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:72
msgid ""
"python -I -m tilelang.tools.compile_only --target cuda --output_file out.cu "
"example.py\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:76
msgid ""
"extern \"C\" __global__ void __launch_bounds__(64, 1) add_kernel(const "
"half_t* __restrict__ A, const half_t* __restrict__ B, half_t* __restrict__ "
"C) {\n"
"  C[((int)threadIdx.x)] = (A[((int)threadIdx.x)] + B[((int)threadIdx.x)]);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:82
msgid "How the Input Is Processed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:84
msgid ""
"The input file is imported as a regular Python module, so its top-level code "
"runs. Keep examples compile-only: define kernels, do not launch them or "
"allocate tensors at import time. Running the CLI with `python -I` (isolated "
"mode) is recommended, and is how Compiler Explorer invokes it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:88
msgid ""
"The first `@tilelang.jit` function or `PrimFunc` in module order is "
"selected. Objects are inspected in definition order, so a `PrimFunc` defined "
"before a `@tilelang.jit` kernel wins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:91
msgid ""
"The kernel is lowered but never device-compiled or executed, so no tensor "
"arguments are needed and no GPU is touched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:94
msgid "CLI Reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:96
msgid ""
"python -I -m tilelang.tools.compile_only [--target TARGET] --output_file "
"OUTPUT input_file\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "Argument"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "`input_file`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "Compile-only example file. Imported, never launched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "`--output_file`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid ""
"Required destination for the generated kernel source. Must not name the "
"input file (symlinks to it are also rejected)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "`--target`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "Explicit target. Defaults to `c`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:106
msgid ""
"On success the CLI exits with `0` and writes the source to `--output_file`. "
"On any failure it exits with `1`, prints a single `tilelang compile-only "
"error: ...` line to stderr, and leaves no stale output behind: a previous "
"artifact at `--output_file` is removed before compilation, so a failed rerun "
"cannot leave an earlier run's source for a consumer such as Compiler "
"Explorer to read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:113
msgid "Targets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:115
msgid ""
"Targets must be explicit. `auto` performs device detection and is therefore "
"rejected, as a plain string and in JSON form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:118
msgid ""
"$ python -I -m tilelang.tools.compile_only --target auto --output_file out.c "
"example.py\n"
"tilelang compile-only error: target must be explicit; do not use auto\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "`--target` value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "`c` (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "CPU C source. Works on every wheel, no GPU needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "`cuda`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "CUDA source pinned to `sm_80`, so no device detection happens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "`cuda -arch=sm_90`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid ""
"CUDA source for the given architecture. Options must look like `-key=value`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "`{\"kind\": \"cuda\", \"arch\": \"sm_90\"}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid ""
"JSON target. A bare `{\"kind\": \"cuda\"}` is pinned to `sm_80`; `{\"kind\": "
"\"auto\"}` is rejected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "`auto`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:0
msgid "Rejected: `target must be explicit; do not use auto`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:131
msgid ""
"On wheels without the CUDA codegen FFI (for example macOS Metal wheels), "
"every CUDA target form fails softly with `tilelang compile-only error: CUDA "
"codegen FFI missing (e.g. macOS Metal wheel); use default --target c`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:136
msgid "Error Reporting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:138
msgid ""
"Compile problems are reported as diagnostics on stderr with exit code `1`, "
"not as tracebacks about missing GPUs or drivers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:141
msgid ""
"$ python -I -m tilelang.tools.compile_only --output_file out.c broken.py\n"
"tilelang compile-only error: no @tilelang.jit kernel or PrimFunc found\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:146
msgid ""
"Syntax errors in the input, missing input files, and empty kernels are "
"reported the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:149
msgid "Line Directives"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:151
msgid ""
"When the installed build registers the `tl.emit_line_directives` pass config "
"(`PassConfigKey.TL_EMIT_LINE_DIRECTIVES`), the tool enables it automatically "
"and the generated source carries `#line <n> \"<input_file>\"` directives "
"that map each statement back to the originating line of the example. "
"Compiler Explorer uses these to link generated source to the input pane. "
"Older wheels without the config key simply produce source without `#line` "
"directives; no flag is needed either way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:159
msgid "Programmatic API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:161
msgid "The same functionality is available in Python:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:163
msgid ""
"from tilelang.tools.compile_only import compile_kernel_source\n"
"\n"
"source = compile_kernel_source(add.get_tir())              # default target "
"\"c\"\n"
"cuda_source = compile_kernel_source(add.get_tir(), \"cuda\")  # pinned to "
"sm_80\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:170
msgid ""
"`compile_kernel_source(func, target=\"c\")` lowers a `PrimFunc` (for example "
"from `JITImpl.get_tir()`) and returns the non-empty kernel source string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:172
msgid ""
"`resolve_target(target)` maps a CLI-style target string to the explicit "
"target passed to `lower()`, applying the rules from the table above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:174
msgid ""
"`cuda_codegen_available()` reports whether the installed wheel can lower "
"CUDA targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:177
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:179
msgid ""
"Only the first `@tilelang.jit` kernel or `PrimFunc` in the module is "
"compiled; additional kernels in the same file are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:181
msgid ""
"The output is lowered kernel source, not a compiled binary: nothing is "
"passed to `nvcc`, and PTX/SASS is out of scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/compile_only.md:183
msgid ""
"The input file is executed with the invoking Python interpreter. Treat it "
"like any script you run: `python -I` isolates it from your environment but "
"does not sandbox it."
msgstr ""
